<title>CHILE: Chile Quebrada Blanca copper miners vote to strike.</title>
<headline>Chile Quebrada Blanca copper miners vote to strike.</headline>
<dateline>SANTIAGO 1997-04-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Workers at the Quebrada Blanca copper mine in Chile have voted to reject the company's final pay and go on strike, said a union official on Sunday, quoting the vote supervisors.</p>
<p>The strike is due to start from first shift Wednesday.</p>
<p>Management had offered a one percent pay increase in real terms -- the union had demanded 18 percent.</p>
</text>
